 @ajjames1960   I never said the issue itself was a bottleneck, James, I said that the only reason the overhead issue is that big a problem is that people treat bottlenecks like it's the end of the world. 
Because of that, the advice people on reddit give is "Get the best gpu you can afford, and the worst cpu you can buy that won't bottleneck it". That's terrible advice for many reasons, including but not limited to upgradability, cost, and overall non-gaming performance, and it's why people actually try and run a month old GPU on a 7 years old midrange CPU (R5 2600). That's crazy talk. 

As far as the overhead issue itself goes, the R5 5600 isn't really part of it. Sure, it loses some performance on the 5600, losing to the 4060 by about 10 fps on the same configuration, but it's not a disaster and the B580 w/ 5600 still wins by a mile in performance per dollar. The actual issue comes from CPUs older than Intel 10th gen and Ryzen 3000, like the 2600. And, like I said, running a B580 on a 2600 is crazy talk, that thing is older than some of the people who watched this video !
